From 822bc4c379ca40be540265d2c86e82a518f0a14c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: minseong <minseong7859@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:25:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] configs: SM120_RTX_PRO_4000 trace config (OMMA
 tensor-unit timing)

Tensor unit (HMMA/IMMA/OMMA) latency,II = 29,16, calibrated against
clock64 microbenchmarks of OMMA.SF.16864.F32.E2M1.E2M1.UE4M3.4X on an
RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell: II 16 reproduces 16.0 cycles/OMMA per warp and
4.0 cycles/OMMA per SM; the simulated dependent chain is 35 cycles vs
29.2 measured. Other latencies are unvalidated Ampere (SM86) values.
-trace_omma_reg_groups 1 (full register groups).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../SM120_RTX_PRO_4000/trace.config           | 40 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 gpu-simulator/configs/tested-cfgs/SM120_RTX_PRO_4000/trace.config

diff --git a/gpu-simulator/configs/tested-cfgs/SM120_RTX_PRO_4000/trace.config b/gpu-simulator/configs/tested-cfgs/SM120_RTX_PRO_4000/trace.config
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fb4255e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gpu-simulator/configs/tested-cfgs/SM120_RTX_PRO_4000/trace.config
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# NVIDIA RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell (sm_120) trace-driven latencies.
+# Values not marked MEASURED are UNCERTAIN Ampere (SM86_RTX3070) values.
+-trace_opcode_latency_initiation_int 2,2
+-trace_opcode_latency_initiation_sp 2,1
+-trace_opcode_latency_initiation_dp 64,64
+-trace_opcode_latency_initiation_sfu 21,8
+-trace_opcode_latency_initiation_tensor 29,16
+
+#execute branch insts on spec unit 1
+#<enabled>,<num_units>,<max_latency>,<ID_OC_SPEC>,<OC_EX_SPEC>,<NAME>
+-specialized_unit_1 1,4,4,4,4,BRA
+-trace_opcode_latency_initiation_spec_op_1 4,4
+
+#TEX unit, make fixed latency for all tex insts
+-specialized_unit_2 1,4,200,4,4,TEX
+-trace_opcode_latency_initiation_spec_op_2 200,4
+
+#tensor unit: one per sub-core (4 per SM). HMMA/IMMA/OMMA all use it.
+# OMMA.SF.16864.F32.E2M1.E2M1.UE4M3.4X, MEASURED on this GPU (clock64,
+# results_hw_omma_microbench.txt): dependent-chain 29.2 cycles/OMMA,
+# one warp with independent OMMAs 16.1-16.2 cycles/OMMA, SM 4.00 cycles/OMMA.
+# Initiation interval 16 also matches NVIDIA spec: 1290 sparse FP4 TOPS -> 645
+# dense / (70 SM x 2.232 GHz) ~ 4096 FLOP/clk/SM = 1024/TC; 16384 FLOP/MMA.
+# <latency>,<II> = 29,16 (calibration: experiments/blackwell_omma_port/results/calibration.csv):
+#  - II 16 reproduces HW exactly: 1 warp 16.00 cycles/OMMA, SM 4.000 cycles/OMMA.
+#  - Simulated dependent chain = latency + 6 pipeline cycles = 35.0 (HW 29.2, +20%).
+#    latency 23 would match the dependent chain (29.0) but config latencies 23..26
+#    make the in-order warp issue OMMAs in bursts (1 warp: 17.9-18.3 cycles/OMMA,
+#    HW 16.1); >=27 is stable. 29 keeps 3 cycles of margin from that region.
+# HMMA/IMMA latencies on sm_120 were NOT measured; they get the same values.
+-specialized_unit_3 1,4,29,4,4,TENSOR
+-trace_opcode_latency_initiation_spec_op_3 29,16
+
+#UDP unit, for turing and above
+-specialized_unit_4 1,4,4,4,4,UDP
+-trace_opcode_latency_initiation_spec_op_4 4,1
+
+# OMMA register-file operand model (see trace_driven.cc set_omma_operands):
+# 1 = every register of A(4)/B(2)/C(4)/D(4) groups + SFA + SFB.
+-trace_omma_reg_groups 1
